+/*
+ * TULIP 0278: the vendor pinctrl splits the TLMM into tiles. GPIO 2/3 are in
+ * the SOUTH tile (0x03000000 + 0x100000 + 0x1000 * n = 0x03102000) and GPIO
+ * 66/67 in the NORTH tile (+0x900000 -> 0x03942000). 0271 mapped 0x03002000 /
+ * 0x03042000, which is outside any tile and hangs the AXI bus. The external
+ * pull-ups sit on pm660_l11, which XNU does not power, so only the weak
+ * internal pull-up is left: slow half bit.
+ */
+#define TT_HALF 50
 
